---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service | ctrl-cv" description="The terms for using ctrl-cv.">
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 9, 2026</p>

    <p>These terms govern your use of the ctrl-cv service, provided by ctrl-cv ("we"). By using the service, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the service.</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>ctrl-cv lets you save text from one AI assistant and retrieve it in another, using the Model Context Protocol, and view and delete your saved text ("clips") on the web. ctrl-cv is at an early stage, and features may change or stop at any time.</p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>You sign in with a Google account, and you must be at least 14 years old, or the minimum age for using online services without parental consent where you live. You are responsible for activity under your account and for the AI apps you connect to it.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>You keep ownership of your clips. You allow us to store, process, and transmit them only as needed to provide the service, including sending them to the AI apps you ask to paste them. You are responsible for your clips and for having the right to save and share them. Our <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle them.</p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break the law or infringe the rights of others;</li>
      <li>save or distribute malware, or content that exploits or harms children;</li>
      <li>probe, overload, or disrupt the service, or get around its limits or security;</li>
      <li>access another person's account or clips;</li>
      <li>use the service to attack or manipulate other systems, including through instructions hidden in clips.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free copies and plans</h2>
    <p>Each account gets 30 free copies, with no card and no time limit. After that, you need a paid plan to copy new text. You can still paste, view, and delete your existing clips until they expire. Deleting clips doesn't restore free copies. Plans and prices are shown on our <a href={`${base}/pricing/`}>pricing page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Payment and renewal</h2>
    <p>Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our orders, and handles payment, applicable taxes, and order-related inquiries and returns. Your purchase is also subject to Paddle's <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/buyer-terms">buyer terms</a>.</p>
    <p>A paid plan renews automatically at the end of each monthly or yearly period, and is charged to your payment method until you cancel. The total, including any tax, is shown at checkout. If a payment fails, Paddle may try again, and your plan may end if it keeps failing. We will give you notice before a price change applies to your plan, and you can cancel before it takes effect.</p>

    <h2>Cancellation and refunds</h2>
    <p>You can cancel at any time under Billing in your account. Your plan stays active until the end of the period you have paid for. Refunds are covered by our <a href={`${base}/refund/`}>Refund Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Limits and deletion</h2>
    <p>Clips are deleted automatically 30 days after they are saved. Storage is limited per clip and per account, and your oldest clips are removed first when you reach your account's limit. ctrl-cv is not a backup, so keep your own copy of anything important.</p>

    <h2>AI output</h2>
    <p>Your AI app writes the text that ctrl-cv stores and reads the text that ctrl-cv returns. AI apps can change, shorten, or misread text, and we don't control them. Check clips before relying on them. Your use of an AI app is subject to its provider's terms. Text in a clip can influence an AI that reads it, so only paste clips you trust.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>ctrl-cv depends on services we don't control, including Google sign-in, Paddle, and AI apps. We aren't responsible for them, and changes to them may affect ctrl-cv.</p>

    <h2>Suspension and ending use</h2>
    <p>You can stop using ctrl-cv at any time and delete your clips on the web. We may suspend or end access if you break these terms, to protect the service or others, or if we discontinue the service. If we discontinue a paid plan, we will refund the unused part of any period you have already paid for.</p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, ctrl-cv is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind. We don't promise that it will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that clips will never be lost.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, ctrl-cv is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages, or for lost data or profits. Nothing in these terms limits rights or liability that can't be limited under the law that applies to you.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. When we do, we will change the date above, and for significant changes we will give notice through the service. If you keep using ctrl-cv after a change takes effect, you accept the updated terms.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:help@ctrl-cv.io">help@ctrl-cv.io</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>
